      "title": "Anne Aly reveals she has received 19 death threats in the last week alone",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/anne-aly-reveals-she-has-received-19-death-threats-last-week-alone-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>After an opposition MP says she should be ‘shamed and stoned’, the federal minister hits back at ‘racist and misogynistic’ language</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Anne Aly has condemned as “racist” and “misogynistic” comments in parliament calling for her to be “stoned in the square” – while revealing she has received 19 death threats in the last week alone.</p><p>The Gold Coast Liberal National MP Angie Bell, the member for Moncrieff, told the House of Representatives that Aly, the small business minister, and the prime minister should be “shamed and stoned in the square” over a decision made by the tax office.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/anne-aly-reveals-she-has-received-19-death-threats-last-week-alone-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-13T09:13:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "Child safety staff determined to send Elizabeth Struhs home with parents despite doctors’ concerns, inquest hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/elizabeth-struhs-inquest-death-religious-cult-saints-child-safety-witness-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Queensland coronial inquest into death of eight-year-old girl continues after 14 members of religious sect were convicted of her manslaughter</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>It was impossible to change the mind of child safety staff after they had decided to send Elizabeth Struhs home with her parents despite some of her doctors’ concerns, a police officer has told a coronial inquest into the young girl’s death.</p><p>Child safety staff decided in 2019 that it would be “more detrimental” to not return Elizabeth, aged six at the time, to her Toowoomba home upon her discharge from hospital after suffering a coma due to diabetic ketoacidosis,<strong> </strong>a Queensland coroner heard.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/13/elizabeth-struhs-inquest-death-religious-cult-saints-child-safety-witness-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
